    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\widehat{\\ell}(\\mathbf{z}) $ is the likelihood function evaluated at the MLE for the full model, and $ \\widehat{\\ell}_{r}(\\mathbf{z}) $ is the maximum of the likelihood function for the restricted model under which r parameters of the full model are assigned fixed values. Under appropriate conditions, the LR test statistic is approximately distributed as $ \\chi_{r}^{2} $, i.e., as a $ \\chi^{2} $ distribution with r degrees of freedom (Wald 1943); see Appendix 4.",
